<ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">friendly-effects</ansi>

Helpful spells have a target scope. Single-target spells help the named
member; if no name is given, they help the caster. Minor Heal All helps the
caster's present company: its leader and attached living companions, even
without a player party. Temporary charms and pets are not company targets.

  <ansi fg="command">cast heal [member]</ansi>
  Minor Heal costs 3 mana and restores 2 to 6 health to one patient.
  <ansi fg="command">cast healall</ansi>
  Minor Heal All costs 6 mana and restores 2 to 6 health to each patient.
  Both take two rounds of chanting. Healers choose them automatically in
  battle, with the same eligibility and costs; cast by hand outside battle.

Healing stops at each patient's wound limit. Minor Heal, Minor Heal All
and first aid can help a downed player above -10 health. A fallen companion
needs resurrection, and cannot be healed back onto its feet. Other helpful
spells require living targets.

A chant holds its starting targets. Movement, death, dismissal, expired or
transferred charms, and lost membership remove targets before the effect
lands. A new arrival or newly revived member is not added during the chant.
Moving the caster cancels that cast's target set. Mana is charged once at
start. If no one is left to help, the spell fades with
"Your spell finds no one left to help", and the mana stays spent.

Company-wide support never automatically includes other players' companies.
Single-target support can explicitly name another patient beside you,
but not anyone fighting in someone else's battle: its foes, its player,
or that player's companions. Neither spells nor first aid help either side
of a battle you are not part of. You are told the patient is
"caught up in another battle", and one drawn into a battle mid-chant is
dropped.
Allied/area group support requires a consent provider; absent that, it stays
within the caster's company. Harmful spells keep their battle boundaries.

See <ansi fg="command">help cast</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help strategy</ansi>,
<ansi fg="command">help wounds</ansi>, and <ansi fg="command">help resurrect</ansi>.
